We can use PAC CLI to check a Power Platform solution for potential issues and best-practice violations.
ex:
    pac solution check --path "C:\Solutions\BudgetApproval.zip"

pac solution check sends the Dataverse solution project to the Power Apps Checker service, which analyzes solution components 
against Microsoft best-practice rules. Microsoft Power Platform CLI solution command group

It can identify issues related to areas such as:
    
    Performance
    Security
    Maintainability
    Reliability
    Unsupported/problematic patterns
    Problems in JavaScript/web resources
    Custom workflow activities
    SDK message configurations
    Power Automate flows through Flow Checker
    Power Fx through App Checker


So we can do this to unmanaged solution in dev need to download zip and give that path then it will analyze and give the issues.
